INFO:agent.loop:\u26a1 Executing tool: 'knowledge_agent' with arguments: {"source_title": "DOJ indictment and CrowdStrike DNC incident-response account", "source_url": "SRC-001; SRC-002", "text": "SRC-001 is the DOJ-published July 13, 2018 indictment charging 12 Russian military intelligence officers. It alleges GRU Units 26165 and 74455 conducted cyber operations involving staged releases of stolen documents to interfere with the 2016 U.S. election. It specifically alleges that beginning June 2016 conspirators staged and released tens of thousands of stolen emails/documents using fictitious personas “DCLeaks” and “Guccifer 2.0”; Guccifer 2.0 also released documents through Organization 1. It alleges false identities and globally distributed infrastructure were used to conceal Russian connections. It identifies Ivan Yermakov (Unit 26165) as participating in hacks of accounts whose materials were released through DCLeaks and later the DNC email server; Aleksandr Osadchuk (commander, Unit 74455) and Aleksey Potemkin (Unit 74455) as involved in infrastructure, promotion, and releases through DCLeaks and Guccifer 2.0. The indictment alleges Unit 26165 hacked Clinton campaign, DCCC, and DNC networks, used spearphishing, X-Agent/X-Tunnel, stole and exfiltrated documents, and that Unit 74455 assisted with releases and anti-Clinton social-media content. These are indictment allegations, not adjudicated findings in the text returned. SRC-002 is CrowdStrike’s 2020 account of its DNC incident response: it was contacted April 30, 2016, began work May 1, identified two Russian intelligence-affiliated adversaries, COZY BEAR and FANCY BEAR; FANCY BEAR separately breached in April 2016. CrowdStrike says it had high confidence the activity was associated with Russian intelligence, supported by U.S. intelligence and congressional reports, and that its investigation found indicators/circumstantial evidence of exfiltration rather than direct real-time observation. It states remediation occurred June 10-13, 2016 and that the DNC notified the FBI after identifying Russian actors. The source also recounts that an Intelligence Community Assessment said Russian intelligence gained access to DNC networks in July 2015 and GRU exfiltrated large volumes of data; these are quoted/characterized by CrowdStrike."}
